{"type":"message","id":"aa56d615","parentId":"1f539f22","timestamp":"2026-05-19T02:16:37.616Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Error 1101 is consistently returned. This is a Cloudflare Workers error code meaning \"Worker exceeded CPU time\" or something similar. It's likely an issue with the Workers runtime, not with our request format. Let me try different approaches - maybe with a GET request to see the API docs, or try a different endpoint.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully - error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means the worker has hit a limit (CPU time, memory, etc.) or there's a routing issue. Let me try the root endpoint.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n\n错误码 1101 是 Cloudflare Workers 的运行时错误（CPU 超限或路由异常），服务器端问题。尝试访问根路径确认服务状态：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-97426c26-0905-4983-87ae-b89841c33b4f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\" -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":17910,"output":199,"cacheRead":256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18365,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779156990729,"responseId":"chatcmpl-e3018bda-2b02-4b38-9461-31b454a948af"}}
